      "sample_id": "7d84cc78086411ebbd5eac1f6bf848b6",
      "question": "Which film has the director born first, A.P.E.X. or Quax In Africa?",
      "gold_answer": "Quax In Africa",
      "gold_doc_ids": [
        "A.P.E.X.\nA.P.E.X is a 1994 science fiction action film directed by Phillip J. Roth and starring Richard Keats, Mitchell Cox, Lisa Ann Russell, and Marcus Aurelius. The plot concerns a group of scientists who explore the past using robotic probes known as the A.P.E.X or\" Advanced Prototype Exploration units\".",
        "Quax in Africa\nQuax in Africa is a German comedy adventure film produced in 1943/ 44 and released in 1947, directed by Helmut Weiss and starring Heinz Rühmann, Hertha Feiler and Lothar Firmans. It is a sequel to the 1941 film\" Quax the Crash Pilot\".",
        "Phillip J. Roth\nPhillip J. Roth( born June 10, 1959) is an American film producer, director and screenwriter who is known for making low- budget films. He is the founder of the Unified Film Organization( UFO) in America and Bulgaria, which have released various action and science fiction films for television and home video markets.",
        "Helmut Weiss\nHelmut Weiss( January 25, 1907 – January 13, 1969) was a German actor, screenwriter and film director. He was notable for directing\" Tell the Truth\" the first film produced in what was to become the future West Germany after the Second World War. It was made in Hamburg in the British Zone of Occupation. Much of the film had already been made at the UFA studios in Berlin shortly before the arrival of the Red Army, but Weiss dramatically re-shot it. The film was significant in its use of outdoor locations in common with other post-war rubble films."
      ],
