      "sample_id": "f998c58c091b11ebbdaeac1f6bf848b6",
      "question": "Are both movies, Naked Tango and Algiers (Film), from the same country?",
      "gold_answer": "yes",
      "gold_doc_ids": [
        "Naked Tango\nNaked Tango is a 1991 American- Argentine erotic drama film written and directed by Leonard Schrader and starring Vincent D'Onofrio, Mathilda May, Esai Morales and Fernando Rey. The choreography was created by Carlos Rivarola.",
        "Algiers (film)\nAlgiers is a 1938 American drama film directed by John Cromwell and starring Charles Boyer, Sigrid Gurie, and Hedy Lamarr. Written by John Howard Lawson, the film is about a notorious French jewel thief hiding in the labyrinthine native quarter of Algiers known as the Casbah. Feeling imprisoned by his self- imposed exile, he is drawn out of hiding by a beautiful French tourist who reminds him of happier times in Paris. The Walter Wanger production was a remake of the successful 1937 French film\" Pépé le Moko\", which derived its plot from the Henri La Barthe novel of the same name. \" Algiers\" was a sensation because it was the first Hollywood film starring Hedy Lamarr, whose beauty became the main attraction for film audiences. The film is notable as one of the sources of inspiration to the screenwriters of the 1942 Warner Bros. film\" Casablanca\", who wrote it with Hedy Lamarr in mind as the original female lead. Charles Boyer's depiction of the main character, Pepe Le Moko, inspired the Warner Bros. animated character, Pepé Le Pew. In 1966, the film entered the public domain in the United States because the claimants did not renew its copyright registration in the 28th year after publication."
      ],
